                <pb facs="0799" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg785"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Boutwell, Secretary of the Treasury, to Mr.
                        Grinnell, collector.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-05-14"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 14,
                        1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit herewith a copy of a letter
                    under date of the 13th instant, from the Secretary of State, relative to
                    representations made to him by the Spanish minister, in regard to the alleged
                    fitting out of certain steamers at your port under suspicious circumstances. You
                    will please exercise special vigilance to prevent the sailing of any vessel from
                    your port in violation of law, and keep the Department fully advised respecting
                    the matter.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. S. BOUTWELL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                            Treasury.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. H. Grinnell</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Collector of Customs.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
